Proposal: record team composition on game_started, so replay retention can be split into
co-op and adversarial play. DRAFT for Shombith's review; not applied, not compiled, not run in
the Unity editor (no editor was reachable). Apply with:  git apply Docs/Analytics/proposals/team_composition_fields.patch

What it adds to game_started, from the LOCAL player's side:
  domain                    the local player's domain (Domains enum name)
  humans_on_my_domain       humans on that domain, the local player included
  humans_on_other_domains   humans on any other domain (AI excluded)
  co-op = no humans on other domains; adversarial = humans on other domains and none beside you;
  mixed = both. Omitted when there is no local player (a count of "other" would read as all
  opponents).

PostHog only, on purpose. AnalyticsServiceFacade sends one identical payload to UGS and PostHog,
and UGS needs every parameter declared by hand in the Event Manager (permanent rows, 1,500 cap).
AnalyticsServiceFacade.PostHogOnlyParameters lists the three names and UgsAnalyticsSink skips them,
so UGS is unchanged and nothing needs declaring there. If you would rather have them in UGS too,
delete that set and the skip, and declare them in the dashboard (see ugs_step1_parameters.csv).

game_completed is NOT changed: it joins to game_started on (distinct_id, match_id), and the
replay queries read play type from game_started.

Verify after applying: play a 2-human match on two domains and a 2-human match on one; the
game_started rows should show humans_on_other_domains 1 and 0. Until then every multi-human
play is "multi_human_unknown" in Docs/Analytics/queries/replay_retention.sql.

